  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to consider the differences between outcomes and a reference value (zero, since no sure outcome exists), compute the mean of these differences weighted by probabilities, and prefer the lottery with the more favorable mean difference. In this case, both lotteries have the same expected value (2700), so the mean differences are equal — the reason would be indifferent. However, the verbal report does not mention any reference value, differences from a reference, or any calculation of mean differences. Instead, it expresses a normative attitude toward risk ('risiko macht erfolgreich') — a preference for risk, not a calculation-based preference based on differences from a reference. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as defined. The justification is conceptually different and does not align with the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the decision reason was not used.",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
